-- title:
--   The rational median routine makes no independence-oracle calls
-- statement:
--   Let $v$ be any finite list of rational numbers. The median routine sorts by repeated insertion, selects the entry at index $\lfloor|v|/2\rfloor$, and returns zero if no entry exists. Let $\operatorname{oracleCalls}$ be the sum of the two independence-oracle coordinates of the computation’s charge vector. Then
--   $$\operatorname{oracleCalls}(\operatorname{medianRational}(v))=0.$$
--   The input may be empty or have even length.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/ResourceBound.lean#L93-L111

